# Contributor Covenant Code of Conduct

## Our Pledge

We, as members, contributors, and maintainers of the Codexeron community, pledge to make participation in our project a welcoming, respectful, and professional experience for everyone.

We are committed to fostering an open, inclusive, and collaborative environment where developers of all backgrounds and experience levels can contribute with confidence.

---

# Our Standards

Examples of behavior that contributes to a positive environment include:

- Being respectful and professional.
- Giving constructive feedback.
- Accepting constructive criticism gracefully.
- Helping new contributors.
- Sharing knowledge openly.
- Respecting different viewpoints.
- Prioritizing security and code quality.
- Communicating clearly and honestly.

---

# Unacceptable Behavior

The following behaviors are unacceptable:

- Harassment or discrimination.
- Personal attacks.
- Offensive or abusive language.
- Trolling or intentionally disruptive behavior.
- Publishing private information without permission.
- Spam or malicious content.
- Security abuse or exploitation.
- Submitting intentionally harmful code.

---

# Our Responsibilities

Project maintainers are responsible for:

- Reviewing contributions fairly.
- Enforcing community standards.
- Maintaining a respectful environment.
- Protecting contributors from harassment.
- Making moderation decisions transparently.

---

# Reporting Issues

If you experience or witness unacceptable behavior, please contact:

community@codexeron.com

For security-related matters, please refer to SECURITY.md.

---

# Enforcement

Project maintainers may:

- Remove inappropriate comments.
- Close disruptive issues.
- Reject malicious Pull Requests.
- Temporarily restrict participation.
- Permanently ban users who repeatedly violate this Code of Conduct.

Enforcement decisions will be made fairly and consistently.

---

# Scope

This Code of Conduct applies to:

- GitHub repositories
- Discussions
- Issues
- Pull Requests
- Documentation
- Community events
- Official communication channels

---

# Our Values

At Codexeron, we value:

- Professionalism
- Transparency
- Security
- Collaboration
- Innovation
- Continuous learning
- Respect
- Open communication

